{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I now have a full picture of the structure. Key assets:\n\n**Components (02)**:\n- Button (1:473) — Type=Primary, State=Default, 200×64\n- Text Field (1:495) — State=Empty, 380×78\n- Status Bar (49:130) — 430×44\n- Home Indicator (49:141) — 430×34\n\n**Media (04)**:\n- Foodgo_Wordmark / Dark (1:196), 171×60\n- Foodgo_Wordmark / White (1:204), 171×60\n- Splash_Burger_Stack (1:209), 220×258\n- Avatar_Neutral (1:214), 120×120\n- Burger_Cheeseburger_Wendys (1:224), 177×180\n- Burger_Veggie (1:229), 180×180\n- Burger_Chicken (1:234), 180×165\n- Burger_Fried_Chicken (1:239), 180×125\n- Burger_Exploded_Custom (1:244), 176×240\n- Topping_Tomato (1:252) 100×83, Topping_Onions (1:257) 100×98, Topping_Pickles (1:262) 100×66, Topping_Bacon (1:267) 100×100, Topping_Cheese (1:272) 100×100, Topping_Mushroom (1:277) 100×80, Topping_Avocado (1:282) 100×82\n- Side_Fries (1:290) 100×67, Side_Coleslaw (1:295) 100×100, Side_Salad (1:300) 100×71, Side_Onion_Rings (1:305) 100×100, Side_Mozzarella_Sticks (1:310) 75×100\n- Card_Mastercard (1:318) 100×61, Card_Visa (1:323) 64×64\n- Icons: Home (1:331), User (1:335), Chat (1:339), Heart (1:343), Search (1:347), Filter (1:351), Back (1:355), Chevron Right (1:359), Star (1:363), Settings (1:367), Lock (1:371), Edit (1:375), Sign Out (1:379), Send (1:383), Plus (1:387), Minus (1:393), Check (1:398), Menu (1:404) — all 24×24\n\nI need to inspect the components more closely to understand what they look like — especially the Button, Text Field, Status Bar, Home Indicator, and the icons. Let me get design context for key components. Also need to check how images (rounded-rectangle with image fills) are structured — the Splash_Burger_Stack (1:209) is a rounded-rectangle, presumably with image fill. When I clone these, the image fill will be cloned as well.\n\nStrategy for building:\n1. Use `figma.importComponentByKeyAsync` — but wait, components are in the same file, so I can just use `figma.getNodeById` and clone.\n2. The brief says \"Copy Components and Media into your own new Figma file\" but per benchmark instructions, the delivery is the 03 · Workspace page in this assigned copy. So I can reference/clone nodes directly within the same file (clone from Media page into Workspace). Actually cloning nodes across pages within the same file is fine.\n\nDesign decisions:\n- Viewport 430 × 932 per frame.\n- Colors: brand red #EF2A39, dark brown #3C2F2F. I'll define a palette:\n  - Background: #FFFFFF or light warm gray #F6F5F3? Let me think about the Foodgo reference design (this is based on a known Foodgo app design from a Figma community file). The classic Foodgo design uses a cream/off-white background (#F4F4F4 or similar), dark brown text, red accents.\n  - My palette:\n    - ink #3C2F2F (primary text)\n    - brand red #EF2A39 (primary actions, accents)\n    - neutral-100 #F5F4F2 (page background)\n    - surface #FFFFFF (cards)\n    - muted text #9C9891 or #A0A0A0\n    - divider #ECEAE7\n    - star/rating color: #FFC529 or amber\n    - success green #34A853 or #22A45D\n    - disabled #E5E2DE\n  - Dark screens: Splash could be dark brown (#3C2F2F) background with white wordmark and red accents. That would look striking and use the wordmark/white asset.\n\nTypography scale (Roboto):\n- Display: Lobster only for wordmark (but use supplied wordmark images instead of typing)\n- H1: 28 SemiBold\n- H2: 22 SemiBold\n- H3: 18 SemiBold\n- Body: 15 Regular / 14\n- Caption: 12 Regular\n- Price: 22 Bold\n\nNote: \"For the font Inter, style is 'Semi Bold'\" — for Roboto it's \"Medium\", \"Bold\", \"Regular\". Roboto styles: Thin, Light, Regular, Medium, Bold, Black. Need `loadFontAsync({family:\"Roboto\", style:\"Regular\"})` etc.\n\nPrototype links:\n- 01_Splash → after delay (or on click) → 02_Home. \"auto-advances\" — use After delay 2000ms → navigate to 02_Home. In Figma prototype, \"After delay\" trigger is available via `action = {type: \"NODE\", destinationId, navigation: \"NAVIGATE\", transition...}` with trigger `{type: \"AFTER_DELAY\", timeout: 2000}`.\n- 02_Home: each menu item → its product frame; Profile tab → 10; Support tab → 11.\n- 03: back → 02; Order Now → 07.\n- 04–06: back → 02 (Order Now entry only).\n- 07: back → 03; Order Now → 08.\n- 08: back → 07; Pay Now → 09.\n- 09: Go Back → 02_Home. (Dialog over payment: the 09 frame contains the payment screen content behind a dimmed scrim and a dialog. \"Presentation: dialog over 08_Payment; Payment stays behind it\" — so frame 09 itself shows the payment screen with an overlay on top. I can build 09 as a copy of 08's content with scrim + dialog, or simpler: put a scrim + dialog on top of a duplicate. Since screens are separate frames, I'll rebuild: 09 frame = payment screen (cloned content) + scrim + success dialog. Easiest approach: build 08 fully, then clone 08 into 09 frame, add scrim and dialog on top.)\n- 10: back → 02.\n- 11: back → 02.\n\nComponent structure to build (reusable components on Workspace page):\n- Bottom Nav Bar (with variants? maybe just one component with current tab). Since \"current tab must match the frame\" — Home is the only frame with bottom nav? Actually 02_Home is the only screen with main navigation. Product screens have back navigation. So bottom nav only on 02_Home. I'll still make it a component.\n- App Header (back + search) component — used on product/customize/payment/profile/chat screens. With title maybe. I'll create a \"Header Bar\" component with back button and search button.\n- Chip (category) component with selected/unselected states.\n- Menu Item Card component.\n- Rating Badge component (star + value).\n- Portion stepper component (minus, value, plus).\n- Spice level selector component.\n- Topping card / side card component with added state.\n- Payment method row component.\n- Chat bubble component (agent / customer).\n- Profile row component.\n- Button: reuse provided Button symbol (1:473). Also create