ld in Workspace page (2003:2):\nLayout: place frames in two rows: 01-06 top row, 07-11 second row, with 100px gaps. Coordinates: frame width 430, gap 120. Row y=0 and y=1100.\n\nFirst, I'll create my own component set in Workspace (to the side, e.g., x=-2000 or below the frames area — maybe at y=1400+ area). Components to create:\n1. Tag/Rating badge\n2. Chip (category) — component set with State=Default/Selected\n3. Favourite toggle (heart) — Default/Filled\n4. Menu card\n5. Stepper (portion)\n6. Spice selector\n7. Topping card (default/added)\n8. Payment method row (default/selected)\n9. Toggle switch (on/off)\n10. Chat bubble agent/customer\n11. Profile list row\n12. Header bar (back + search + optional title)\n13. Bottom nav\n14. Primary button — instantiate provided Button symbol? The provided Button is a component instance source (symbol 1:473 with text \"Button\"?). Let me check its design context. I could create my own button component that matches its specs (height 64, primary red, radius). The brief says \"a default Button\" is FIXED — meaning the provided Button component exists and I should use it. \"Reuse the components in 02 · Components\". So for primary CTA buttons I should use instances of the provided Button component (1:473), overriding the Label text property.\n\nLet me now fetch design context for the Button, Text Field, Status Bar, Home Indicator. Also maybe one icon and the wordmark to understand colors.\n\nActually, to keep it efficient, I'll fetch: 1:473 (Button), 1:495 (Text Field), 49:130 (Status Bar), 49:141 (Home Indicator). The icons I'll just instance and recolor. The wordmark 1:196 is a frame/vector outline, fill presumably dark; white variant for dark backgrounds.\n\nAlso need to inspect the Workspace page 2003:2 metadata to see if empty.\n\nLet me do these in parallel: get_design_context for 1:473, 1:495, 49:130, 49:141, and get_metadata for 2003:2.\n\nWait — the instruction says \"IMPORTANT: After you call this tool, you MUST call 