er topping, name override).\n15. SideCard set: Default/Added.\n16. MenuCard component: image rect override, category/name/rating text overrides, fav toggle — fav state differs (cheeseburger on). Variants Fav=Off/On? The heart inside card — instance of FavToggle. Override per instance via nested instance property... nested instance fill overrides are possible but fiddly. I'll make MenuCard variants: Favourite=Off/On.\n\nThis is getting big. Manageable: I'll write a build script that creates all components in one call (~a lot of code). Maybe split: Call A = core atoms (chips, hearts, toggles, icon buttons, rating, stepper, spice), Call B = cards (menu, topping, side, payment row, chat bubble, profile rows, header bars, bottom nav), then screens in calls C..H, then prototype links call I, screenshots J.\n\nTo reduce complexity, build components as auto-layout frames with fixed sizes where needed.\n\nColors:\n- bg: #F7F5F2 (247,245,242)\n- surface: #FFFFFF\n- ink: #3C2F2F\n- muted: #8A8280 (138,130,128)? slightly warm gray\n- faint: #B8B0AD\n- line: #EDE9E6\n- red: #EF2A39\n- redDark: #D61F2E (pressed)\n- redSoft: #FDEBEC (destructive bg, red tint)\n- amber: #F5A623? rating star — I'll use #FF9F2D or classic #FFC529. Choose #F6A31A? Let me pick #FFA41B.\n- success: #2EA26B\n- scrim: rgba(60,47,47,0.55)\n\nFonts to load: Roboto: Regular, Medium, SemiBold, Bold. (Roboto has \"SemiBold\" style — as seen in Button label fontName {family:\"Roboto\", style:\"SemiBold\"}.) Good — confirmed by component inspection.\n\nLet me now also think about the icon IDs:\n- Icon / Home 1:331\n- Icon / User 1:335\n- Icon / Chat 1:339\n- Icon / Heart 1:343\n- Icon / Search 1:347\n- Icon / Filter 1:351\n- Icon / Back 1:355\n- Icon / Chevron Right 1:359\n- Icon / Star 1:363\n- Icon / Settings 1:367\n- Icon / Lock 1:371\n- Icon / Edit 1:375\n- Icon / Sign Out 1:379\n- Icon / Send 1:383\n- Icon / Plus 1:387\n- Icon / Minus 1:393\n- Icon / Check 1:398\n- Icon / Menu 1:404\n\nMedia rects (image fills):\n- Splash_Burger_Stack 1:209 (220×258)\n- Foodgo wordmark components: 1:196 Dark, 1:204 White (171×60) — these are COMPONENTS (symbol). Instancing keeps vector outline. \n- Avatar_Neutral 1:214 component 120×120\n- Burger_Cheeseburger_Wendys 1:224 (177×180)\n- Burger_Veggie 1:229 (180×180)\n- Burger_Chicken 1:234 (180×165)\n- Burger_Fried_Chicken 1:239 (180×125)\n- Burger_Exploded_Custom 1:244 (176×240)\n- Topping images: 1:252 Tomato, 1:257 Onions, 1:262 Pickles, 1:267 Bacon, 1:272 Cheese, 1:277 Mushroom, 1:282 Avocado\n- Side images: 1:290 Fries, 1:295 Coleslaw, 1:300 Salad, 1:305 Onion Rings, 1:310 Mozzarella\n- Card_Mastercard 1:318 (100×61), Card_Visa 1:323 (64×64)\n\nFor image rect cloning: clone the rounded-rectangle node, then `resize()` and keep imageScaleMode \"FIT\" (clone preserves fill incl. scaleMode). The guide says use Fit, keep proportions.\n\nAvatar: instance component 1:214, resize to 48/96 — component instance resize works; inner may be scale? It's a symbol with a rect image probably; resizing instance to 48×48 should scale contents? Instance resize scales the component's size; children with constraints... may not scale image nicely. Safer: instance + resize + set cornerRadius on instance? If inner rect is 120×120 fixed, resizing instance to 48 would clip/scale? Instances resize their bounding box; children with SCALE constraint scale proportionally. Unknown constraints. Alternative: clone the component node itself (clone of COMPONENT gives another component? cloning a component node creates a copy that is also a component? Actually `component.clone()` returns a new component). I can't put a raw component copy in frames — actually you CAN'T place a COMPONENT node inside a frame? You can (it becomes... no, components live on canvas; placing component inside frame is not allowed—actually components CAN be nested? No. Instances only). Hmm: `figma.createComponentFromNode(existingComponentNode)`? That converts. Simplest: instance it and resize; 