uns`? Let me recall: In the Plugin API, prototype interactions are on nodes: `node.absoluteRenderBounds`... For interactions: `node.reactions` (React on PrototypeRestart?). The API: `ReactionsProperty`: `node.reactions = [{ trigger: {type:\"AFTER_DELAY\", timeout: 2000}, action: {type:\"NODE\", destinationId: \"2:xyz\", navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition: {type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration: 0.3}} }]`. Yes — `reactions` is the property on SceneNode for prototype interactions. Trigger types: {type:\"ON_TAP\"}, {type:\"AFTER_DELAY\", timeout}. Action {type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation, transition, preserveScroll}. Good.\n\nScrolling: for Home/Customize content overflow: set frame scrollBehavior? \"Home and Customize may scroll vertically\" — optional. I'll design to fit.\n\nOverflow/clipping: frames clipContent true default.\n\nNow — a concern: use_figma calls have 50k char limit each; I'll write compact helper code repeated per call (helpers must be redefined in each call since state doesn't persist). I'll keep a compact helper preamble string reused across calls (~3-4k chars).\n\nHelper preamble (JS):\n```js\nconst C = {red:\"EF2A39\", ink:\"3C2F2F\", bg:\"F7F5F2\", surf:\"FFFFFF\", mut:\"8A8078\", faint:\"BDB4AF\", line:\"EDE8E4\", amber:\"FFA41B\", ok:\"2EA26B\", redSoft:\"FDEBEC\", dark:\"3C2F2F\"};\nconst hex = h => {const n=parseInt(h,16);return {r:((n>>16)&255)/255,g:((n>>8)&255)/255,b:(n&255)/255};};\nconst S = c => [{type:\"SOLID\",color:hex(c)}];\nasync function T(chars, size, style, color, ls){await figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Roboto\",style});const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:\"Roboto\",style};t.characters=chars;t.fontSize=size;t.fills=S(color);return t;}\nfunction F(w,h,fill,r){const f=figma.createFrame();f.resize(w,h);f.fills=fill?S(fill):[];if(r)f.cornerRadius=r;return f;}\nfunction AL(dir,w,h,fill,r,gap,pad){const f=F(w,h,fill,r);f.layoutMode=dir;f.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\";f.counterAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\";f.itemSpacing=gap||0;if(pad){f.paddingLeft=pad[0];f.paddingTop=pad[1];f.paddingRight=pad[2];f.paddingBottom=pad[3];}return f;}\nasync function icon(id,color,size){const src=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);const i=src.createInstance();i.resize(size,size);const col=S(color);for(const n of i.findAll(x=>\"fills\"in x&&x.fills&&x.fills.length&&x.fills[0].type===\"SOLID\"))n.fills=col;return i;}\nasync function imgRect(id,w,h,r){const src=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);const n=src.clone();n.resize(w,h);if(r!==undefined)n.cornerRadius=r;n.name=src.name;return n;}\n```\nWait: for icons — icon components are vectors inside; fills might be on vector children. findAll over instance children works. Some icon vectors may have strokes not fills! \"Plus / Minus / Check / Menu are simple line glyphs\" — line glyphs might use strokes. I'll handle both: set strokes color too if strokes present.\n\nimgRect: clone of rounded-rectangle with image fill; resize keeps imageScaleMode FIT and scales? Image fill with scaleMode FIT adapts to node size — good. Corner radius preserved (already some). \n\nFor wordmark: `const wm = (await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"1:196\")).createInstance(); wm.resize(w, 60*w/171);` If inner vector constraints don't scale, it may look off — need to check inner structure. Wordmark is a component 171×60 containing likely a vector with constraints SCALE. I'll check in inspection call.\n\nAvatar similar check.\n\nAlright — inspection Call A (read-only): inspect 1:214 (Avatar), 1:196 (wordmark dark), 1:209 (splash rect fill details incl scaleMode), 1:224 (burger rect fill), 1:331 (Icon/Home inner), 1:393 (Icon/Minus inner — check strokes), 1:363 (Icon/Star), 1:318 (Card_Mastercard fill), and fonts availability check (listAvailableFontsAsync filtered Roboto/Lobster). Return JSON.\n\nThen Call B: create paint styles + text styles + atoms (components). Then Call C: more components (cards, nav, headers, bubbles). Then screens D: Splash + Home. E: products 03-06 (script generates 4 from data). 