{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All composite components created. New IDs:\n- hbSearch 2010:58, hbSettings 2010:74, hbMenu 2010:87\n- mcOn 2010:138, mcOff 2010:159\n- topAdd 2010:180, topDef 2010:187\n- sideAdd 2010:194, sideDef 2010:201\n- nav 2010:98\n\nNow build screens. Call C: Splash (01) + Home (02). Layout plan from summary: Row1 y=0: 01 x=0, 02 x=550, 03 x=1100, 04 x=1650, 05 x=2200, 06 x=2750; Row2 y=1050: 07 x=0, 08 x=550, 09 x=1100, 10 x=1650, 11 x=2200.\n\nShared helpers for screens:\n- screen(name,x,y,bg) → frame 430×932\n- statusBar(dark) → instance of 49:130, fills=[], recolor children black (light screens) or white (dark). StatusBar children: \"9:41\" text + glyphs. Recolor: for text set fills; glyphs vector fills.\n- homeInd(dark) → instance of 49:141, fills=[], bar color black/white.\n\nFor Home (02):\n- bg C.bg\n- status black at y0\n- header row y 60: avatar 48 + wordmark dark (height 40, width 114) — layout: absolute positioning. avatar x24 y60; wordmark x centered: (430-114)/2=158, y 64.\n- greeting \"Order your favourite food!\" Title/XL at x24 y 128, width 382 wrap → 2 lines? \"Order your favourite food!\" at 28 Bold ≈ 26 chars × ~15px = 340px → fits 1 line at 382. Maybe 1 line. OK.\n- search row y ~ 176: input search instance resized 314 wide + filter button 56 (white, radius 20, filter icon red 20).\n- chips y 248: 4 chips.\n- grid y 308: 2×2 MenuCards: gap 16. Cards 183×242. Rows: 242×2+16 = 500 → ends 808. Nav at 848. OK.\n- nav instance y 848.\n- home indicator y 898 (932-34).\n\nData for cards:\n1. Cheeseburger / Wendy's Burger / 4.9 — mcOn, img burgerC\n2. Hamburger / Veggie Burger / 4.8 — mcOff, img burgerV\n3. Hamburger / Chicken Burger / 4.6 — mcOff, img burgerCh\n4. Hamburger / Fried Chicken Burger / 4.5 — mcOff, img burgerF\n\nOverrides per card instance: Photo fill, Category text, Name text, rating Value text.\n\nMenuCard instance structure: [Img[Photo, HeartButton instance], Category, Name, Rating[star,Value]]. findOne by name.\n\nChips: chip instances with text override: the Chip component — from B1: chip AL H padding 20/10? I recall Chip: padding H20 V10? I set padding 20 x, 10 y? In B1 I set: chip comps with layoutMode HORIZONTAL, padding L/R 20, T/B 10? Summary doesn't say exact. Chip Selected: red bg, white text; Default: white bg, line stroke, ink text. Text child \"Label\". I'll override characters.\n\nTo be safe with instance text override: `inst.findOne(n=>n.type===\"TEXT\").characters=\"...\"`.\n\nSplash (01):\n- bg ink\n- red glow: ellipse 320 at center behind burger, fill red opacity 0.25, LAYER_BLUR 120.\n- wordmark white instance 1:204 resized to 240 wide (h auto 84). Wordmark original 171×60 → 240 wide → h 84. y 300.\n- Splash_Burger_Stack clone: original 220×258 → 240×281. y 420? center x (430-240)/2=95. y 430.\n- status white, indicator white.\n- Auto-advance: add in proto step.\n\nAlso brief says Splash: Foodgo wordmark + Splash_Burger_Stack. Good.\n\nAvatar: 1:214 instance rescale(48/120=0.4).\n\nWordmark dark: 1:196 instance resize(114,40). SCALE constraints — resize works.\n\nNow write Call C. Include helpers + Splash + Home. Also keep instance names for proto step: name menu cards \"card:03\" etc.? For prototype step I'll need references to nodes. I'll return key node IDs (nav tabs, cards, buttons) from each screen call so proto step can link.\n\nReturn IDs: splash frame, home frame, card instances ×4, navProfileTab, navSupportTab.\n\nFor status bar recolor: instance children — find all TEXT and VECTOR descendants, set fills to white or black. Also glyphs may be boolean/vector. Use findAll on instance.\n\nHome indicator: instance fills=[] (white bg removed), bar vector recolor.\n\nLet me now write Call C carefully.\n\nCode:\n\n```js\nconst P=figma.root.children.find(p=>p.id===\"2003:2\");\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(P);\nawait Promise.all([\"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"SemiBold\",\"Bold\"].map(s=>figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Roboto\",style:s})));\nconst H=h=>{const n=parseInt(h,16);return{r:(n>>16&255)/255,g:(n>>8&255)/255,b:(n&255)/255}};\nconst C={red:\"EF2A39\",ink:\"3C2F2F\",bg:\"F7F5F2\",surf:\"FFFFFF\",mut:\"8A8078\",faint:\"BDB4AF\",line:\"EDE8E4\",amber:\"FFA41B\",ok:\"2EA26B\",field:\"F4F0EC\",redSoft:\"FDEBEC\"};\nconst S=h=>[{type:\"SOLID\",color:H(h)}];\nconst sh=(x,y,r,a,c)=>[{type:\"DROP_SHADOW\",color:c?{...H(c),a}:{r:0.23,g:0.17,b:0.17,a},offset:{x,y},radius:r,visible:true,blendMode:\"NORMAL\"}];\nconst TS={};for(const s of figma.getLocalTextStyles())if(s.name.startsWith(\"FG/\"))TS[s.name.slice(3)]=s.id;\nconst T=async(chars,key,color)=>{const t=figma.createText();await t.setTextStyleIdAsync(TS[key]);t.characters=chars;t.fills=S(color);return t;};\nconst IF=h=>[{type:\"IMAGE\",imageHash:h,scaleMode:\"FIT\"}];\nconst GH=async id=>(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id)).fills[0].imageHash;\nasync function ic(id,color,size){...}\nconst M={...all ids...};\nasync function screen(name,x,y,bg){const f=figma.createFrame();f.name=name;f.resize(430,932);f.x=x;f.y=y;f.fills=S(bg);P.appendChild(f);return f;}\nasync function status(f,dark){const sb=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"49:130\")).createInstance();sb.fills=[];f.appendChild(sb);sb.x=0;sb.y=0;const col=dark?\"FFFFFF\":\"3C2F2F\";for(const n of sb.findAll(n=>\"fills\"in n&&Array.isArray(n.fills)&&n.fills.length)){try{n.fills=S(col)}catch(e){}}return sb;}\nasync function hind(f,dark){const hi=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"49:141\")).createInstance();hi.fills=[];f.appendChild(hi);hi.x=0;hi.y=898;const bar=hi.findOne(n=>n.type!==\"INSTANCE\"&&n.type!==\"TEXT\"&&n.height<10);if(bar)bar.fills=S(dark?\"FFFFFF\":\"3C2F2F\");return hi;}\n```\n\nWait — statusBar instance children include a TEXT \"9:41\" (fills black) and vector glyphs (fills). findAll with fills SOLID → recolor all. Fine.\n\nHome indicator: children = rectangle 134×5. findOne type RECTANGLE. \n\nSplash:\n```js\nconst sp=await screen(\"01_Splash\",0,0,C.ink);\nawait status