{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API schema for reactions differs from my memory. From the error message I can extract the correct shapes:\n\n- action type for navigation: the error lists valid types: \"CONDITIONAL\", \"BACK\", \"CLOSE\", \"URL\", \"UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME\", \"SET_VARIABLE\", \"SET_VARIABLE_MODE\" — hmm, \"NODE\" not listed?! Wait: 'BACK' | 'CLOSE' was one enum branch — that's probably for type \"NODE\"? No... The validation shows branches of the action union. None mentions a navigation-to-node action with destinationId. But Figma prototype \"Navigate to\" action IS type \"NODE\" with destinationId... The error says for one branch: `Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE' at [0].action.type` — that's the branch for action.type \"BACK\"/\"CLOSE\". Hmm, so where's the NODE branch? Maybe in this API version, navigate action has a different shape... \n\nWait, the validation error enumerates ALL branches it tried and why each failed. It seems there was NO branch for {type:\"NODE\", destinationId}?? That can't be right. Unless the correct shape for navigating is type \"NODE\" but the branch requires... it says \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation', 'transition'\" — for EVERY branch. If a NODE branch existed with destinationId, it wouldn't error on destinationId for that branch.\n\nHmm wait, maybe in the current API the navigate action type is \"NODE\" but the properties are different... The error message shows all attempted branches; maybe the NODE branch error was truncated? The listed branches:\n1. CONDITIONAL (needs conditionalBlocks)\n2. BACK|CLOSE (no extra props) — my action had type NODE so failed enum\n3. URL (needs url)\n4. UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME (mediaAction...) ×3\n5. transition-related...?\n6. SET_VARIABLE\n7. SET_VARIABLE_MODE\n\nHmm, there's no NODE navigate branch in the list. Maybe navigation to another frame in the new typing API is `type:\"NODE\"` — but it's not in the union?! \n\nWait — maybe the union validation stops listing after some branches... The message is long; maybe I missed it. Between branches there's also: \"Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following...\" — appears twice, that's probably part of a NODE branch that HAS destinationId/navigation/transition! Look: the 5th chunk complains ONLY about transition (`Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing`, invalid enum DISSOLVE, needs direction/matchLayers). It does NOT complain about destinationId/navigation/type for that branch. So the NODE branch exists and my type/navigation/destinationId were fine; only my TRANSITION shape was wrong!\n\nSo correct transition needs: `easing` + (for DISSOLVE maybe no direction?) Hmm: \"Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following, but none matched\" then branches:\n- a transition branch requiring easing (missing) — this is probably DISSOLVE/SMART_ANIMATE branch: {type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration, easing} — needs easing!\n- another branch: MOVE_IN|MOVE_OUT|PUSH|SLIDE_IN|SLIDE_OUT with direction, matchLayers, easing.\n\nSo DISSOLVE transition = {type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration:0.3, easing:{type:...}}. Easing shape: {type:\"EASE_IN_OUT\"}? Figma easing: {type: \"EASE_IN\" | \"EASE_OUT\" | \"EASE_IN_OUT\" | \"LINEAR\" | \"GENTLE\" | \"QUICK\" | \"BOUNCY\" | \"SLOW\" | \"CUSTOM_EASING\", ...}. I'll use {type:\"EASE_OUT\"}? Safe: \"EASE_IN_OUT\" or \"LINEAR\". Hmm valid literals per typings: Easing = { type: 'CUSTOM_CUBIC', ... } | { type: 'EASE_IN'|'EASE_OUT'|'EASE_IN_OUT'|'LINEAR'|'EASE_IN_AND_OUT_AND_BACK'|... }. I'll use {type:\"EASE_IN_OUT\"} — hmm risk. \"LINEAR\" is safest literal.\n\n- trigger: AFTER_DELAY wrong; valid: \"AFTER_TIMEOUT\" with `delay` (not timeout). Also ON_CLICK (not ON_TAP!). So trigger: {type:\"ON_CLICK\"} and {type:\"AFTER_TIMEOUT\", delay:2000}.\n\nWait, did ON_TAP fail too? First chunk: trigger branch: expected ON_CLICK|ON_HOVER|ON_PRESS|ON_DRAG|ON_MEDIA_END received AFTER_DELAY; and another branch AFTER_TIMEOUT with delay. So ON_TAP may be valid or not — error was for the splash line? The first error was at PLUGIN_1_SOURCE:10:38 = the `delay()` call (splash). It validated my whole reactions array for splash: action NODE branch complained only about transition (missing easing), trigger AFTER_DELAY invalid → use AFTER_TIMEOUT with delay. ON_TAP — used in nav() — wasn't reached for splash. To be safe use ON_CLICK (explicitly valid).\n\nSo:\n```js\nconst nav=d=>[{trigger:{type:\"ON_CLICK\"},action:{type:\"NODE\",destinationId:d,navigation:\"NAVIGATE\",transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\",duration:0.3,easing:{type:\"LINEAR\"}}}}];\nconst delay=(d,ms)=>[{trigger:{type:\"AFTER_TIMEOUT\",delay:ms},action:{...same}}];\n```\nHmm \"delay\" value: ms number. OK.\n\nRetry the whole proto call with fixed shapes.","signature":"97220b0ea41f41e0b0230a3e"}],"id":"8ccacb6e-a343-4689-90e6-81e1b5b873bd","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99adcf7d-6023-4cb2-98f0-822f073f5505","uuid":"1ffc17a6-1624-40f8-bda1-b24a3685c8c6","timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:53:58.037Z","thinking_duration_ms":25774}
