{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a Figma product design benchmark: design the complete \"Foodgo\" burger-ordering app inside page \"03 · Workspace\" (node 2003:2) of assigned file https://www.figma.com/design/HLFV6DkE9fZgeCIwE7fLvf/ (fileKey HLFV6DkE9fZgeCIwE7fLvf). Requirements: (1) whoami confirmed account fulinbo@tetras.ai (done earlier); (2) read \"00 · Start Here\" (0:1) brief; (3) follow \"01 · Foundations\" (1:2) visual rules (fixed #EF2A39 brand red + #3C2F2F dark brown, Lobster logotype + Roboto UI, 430×932 viewport); (4) reuse components from \"02 · Components\" (1:3) — Button 1:473 (200×64 red radius 20, label Roboto SemiBold 18 white \"Order Now\"), Text Field 1:495, Status Bar 49:130 (430×44), Home Indicator 49:141 (430×34); (5) reuse media from \"04 · Media\" (1:4); (6) preserve all reference pages untouched; (7) build 11 frames with EXACT names (01_Splash, 02_Home, 03_Product_Cheeseburger, 04_Product_Veggie, 05_Product_Chicken, 06_Product_Fried_Chicken, 07_Customize, 08_Payment, 09_Payment_Success_Overlay, 10_Profile, 11_Support_Chat) + reusable components + prototype connections in 03 · Workspace; (8) verify via get_screenshot of ALL screens, fix visible problems, re-check; (9) finish with assigned file URL, 03·Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations. Every tool call must be preceded in the same assistant message by a line starting exactly `Reasoning summary:`; final response must start `Reasoning summary: ...` then `Final answer:`. Unattended session — resolve routine choices via brief. Workflow: whoami→get_metadata→read-only use_figma→use_figma build→get_screenshot. Use valid Plugin API calls; load fonts before text edits; build in manageable sections.\n\n   Brief content specifics (from 00 · Start Here, captured in prior summary):\n   - Home: avatar, Foodgo wordmark + \"Order your favourite food!\", categories All(selected)/Combos/Sliders/Classic, search \"Search\" + filter, bottom nav Home(current)/Profile→10/Support→11/Favourites(entry only)+central Add(entry only), 4 menu items (image, category, name, rating, favourite toggle; Cheeseburger favourited), each item→its product frame.\n   - Menu data: Cheeseburger · Wendy's Burger · 4.9 · 26 mins · $8.24 → portion 1; Hamburger · Veggie Burger · 4.8 · 14 mins · $9.99 → portion 1; Hamburger · Chicken Burger · 4.6 · 42 mins · $6.24 → portion 2 = $12.48; Hamburger · Fried Chicken Burger · 4.5 · 14 mins · $6.75 → portion 4 = $27.00.\n   - Product pages 03–06: back→02, search, Order Now (only 03→07), image, full name, rating, prep time, description (verbatim texts captured), portion stepper (current portion), price for portion, spicy Mild→Hot with current level.\n   - 07_Customize: back→03, Order Now→08; toppings Tomato/Onions/Pickles/Bacon/Cheese/Mushroom/Avocado, sides Fries/Coleslaw/Salad/Onion Rings/Mozzarella Sticks; added: Tomato, Cheese, Fries; copy \"Customize Your Burger to Your Tastes. Ultimate Experience\"; Burger_Exploded_Custom; portion 2 stepper; spicy level; Total $16.48.\n   - 08_Payment: back→07, Pay Now→09; \"Order summary\" Order $16.48 / Taxes $0.30 / Delivery fees $1.50 / Total $18.28 / Estimated delivery time 15–30 mins; \"Payment methods\" Credit card (Mastercard, 5105 **** **** 0505, current) + Debit card (Visa, 3566 **** **** 0505), only one chosen; \"Save card details for future payments\" toggle ON; Total price $18.28. (Beware source-file errors $16.49/$18.19 — follow brief.)\n   - 09: dialog over 08 (Payment stays behind), success mark, \"Success!\", \"Your payment was successful. A receipt for this purchase has been sent to your email.\", Go Back → 02.\n   - 10_Profile: back→02, settings, avatar, Sophia Patel, sophiapatel@gmail.com, 123 Main St, Apartment 4A, New York, NY, password (masked, locked), Edit Profile, Log out, entries Order history + Payment Details.\n   - 11_Support_Chat: back→02, menu, send; 7 items in order: A \"Hi, how can I help you?\" · C \"Hello, I ordered two Cheeseburger Wendy's Burgers. Can I know how long it will take to arrive?\" · A \"Ok, please let me check!\" · C \"Sure...\" · A \"It'll take 25 minutes to arrive at your address.\" · [26 minutes ago timestamp after agent's third message] · C \"Ok, thank you for your support.\"; input \"Type here...\".\n   - Splash: Foodgo wordmark + Splash_Burger_Stack, auto-advances → 02.\n   - English UI, USD, customer Sophia Patel; Home & Customize may scroll vertically.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via MCP use_figma tool (50k char limit; state does NOT persist between calls — helpers/IDs must be re-declared each call)\n   - CRITICAL: failed use_figma calls roll back atomically (no partial nodes left; no cleanup needed)\n   - CRITICAL: must `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(P)` at the start of every call that creates nodes, else nodes land on figma.currentPage (\"00 · Start Here 设计任务\")\n   - `figma.combineAsVariants(nodes, P)` requires all nodes on page P\n   - `layoutPositioning=\"ABSOLUTE\"` must be set AFTER appendChild to an auto-layout parent\n   - Text nodes INSIDE component instances: setting `.characters` works, but `textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\"` + `resize()` does NOT stick reliably (ProfileField Value stayed 38w→162h). Workaround: build manual rows from scratch\n   - Prototype reactions schema (from validation error): trigger must be ON_CLICK/ON_HOVER/ON_PRESS/ON_DRAG/ON_MEDIA_END or AFTER_TIMEOUT with `delay` (NOT \"ON_TAP\"-untested, NOT \"AFTER_DELAY\"/`timeout`); action `{type:\"NODE\",destinationId,navigation:\"NAVIGATE\"}` accepted but `transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\"...}` rejected — valid transitions are MOVE_IN/MOVE_OUT/PUSH/SLIDE_IN/SLIDE_OUT requiring direction+easing+matchLayers, or omit transition entirely\n   - Fonts: Roboto styles \"Regular\"/\"Medium\"/\"SemiBold\"/\"Bold\"; load per call; Inter \"Semi Bold\" inside provided StatusBar\n   - Image fills: `{type:\"IMAGE\",imageHash,scaleMode:\"FIT\"}`; capture hash from source `fills[0].imageHash`; clone()+resize() for media rects\n   - Icon recoloring: override both fills and strokes recursively on instance children\n   - Avatar_Neutral (1:214): use `inst.rescale(scale)` due to MIN/MIN constraints\n   - Paint styles \"FG/*\" and text styles \"FG/*\" bound via `setTextStyleIdAsync`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Figma file HLFV6DkE9fZgeCIwE7fLvf** (only file; fulinbo@tetras.ai confirmed). Reference pages 0:1, 1:2, 1:3, 1:4 preserved untouched.\n   - **Page 2003:2 \"03 · Workspace\"** — all new content. Screen coordinate plan: Row1 y=0: 01 x=0, 02 x=550, 03 x=1100, 04 x=1650, 05 x=2200, 06 x=2750; Row2 y=1050: 07 x=0, 08 x=550, 09 x=1100, 10 x=1650, 11 x=2200; components zone y 2040–2900.\n   - **SCREEN IDs (all built)**: 01_Splash 2011:147 · 02_Home 2011:165 · 03_Product_Cheeseburger 2012:313 · 04_Product_Veggie 2012:379 · 05_Product_Chicken 2012:445 · 06_Product_Fried_Chicken 2012:511 · 07_Customize 2013:493 · 08_Payment 2013:634 · 09_Payment_Success_Overlay 2014:644 · 10_Profile 2014:693 · 11_Support_Chat 2015:743\n   - **B1 component IDs (masters)**: rating 2007:23, heartOff 2007:31, heartOn 2007:39, chipSel 2007:47, chipDef 2007:49, ibBack 2007:53, ibSearch 2007:58, ibSettings 2007:67, ibMenu 2007:73, stepper 2007:77, inputSearch 2007:90, inputPill 2007:100, sendBtn 2007:102, profileField 2007:111, linkRow 2007:114, bubA 2007:121, bubC 2007:123, paySel 2007:125, payDef 2007:134; component sets Chip 2007:140, IconButton 2007:141, HeartButton 2007:142, Toggle 2007:143, ChatBubble 2007:144, PaymentRow 2007:145; label text 2007:146.\n   - **B2 component IDs**: HeaderBar set: Type=Search 2010:58, Type=Settings 2010:74, Type=Menu 2010:87; BottomNav 2010:98; MenuCard: Fav=On 2010:138, Fav=Off 2010:159; ToppingCard: State=Added 2010:180, State=Default 2010:187; SideCard: State=Added 2010:194, State=Default 2010:201. burgerHash (1:224): 9ab8bdcbea7d52024fac428da92fb4b98c7fdbbb\n   - **Key instance IDs inside screens**: Home menu cards: 03 2011:211, 04 2011:232, 05 2011:253, 06 2011:274 (named MenuItem/03…06); Home nav instance 2011:295 with tabProfile I2011:295;2010:107, tabSupport I2011:295;2010:120; Home chips: All 2011:203, Combos 2011:205, Sliders 2011:207, Classic 2011:209; Customize PrimaryBtn 2013:630; Payment PrimaryBtn (Pay Now) 2013:709; Overlay GoBackBtn 2014:691, dialog 2014:683; Profile back button I2014:705;2010:75, EditProfileBtn 2014:756; Profile InfoCard now has AddressRow manual row (cardH 211, buttonsY 719, logoutEnd 859).\n   - **Component structures probed**: ProfileField 38×36 AL V (Label TEXT 14h, Value TEXT 18h); LinkRow 382×64 AL H (Title TEXT at x20, \"Icon / Chevron Right\" instance 20×20 at x346); Rating 40×16 (star 16 + Value text at x20); InputPill 322×56 (text child \"Type here...\"); SendBtn 48×48 (send icon 20×20); MenuCard instance internals: Img frame containing Photo RECTANGLE + HeartButton, then Category, Name, Rating (Value text child).\n   - **Header helper code (re-declare per call)**:\n     ```js\n     const P = figma.root.children.find(p => p.id === \"2003:2\");\n     await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(P);\n     await Promise.all([\"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"SemiBold\",\"Bold\"].map(s => figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Roboto\",style:s})));\n     const H=h=>{const n=parseInt(h,16);return{r:(n>>16&255)/255,g:(n>>8&255)/255,b:(n&255)/255}};\n     const C={red:\"EF2A39\",ink:\"3C2F2F\",bg:\"F7F5F2\",surf:\"FFFFFF\",mut:\"8A8078\",faint:\"BDB4AF\",line:\"EDE8E4\",amber:\"FFA41B\",ok:\"2EA26B\",field:\"F4F0EC\",redSoft:\"FDEBEC\"};\n     const S=h=>[{type:\"SOLID\",color:H(h)}];\n     const TS={};for(const s of figma.getLocalTextStyles())if(s.name.startsWith(\"FG/\"))TS[s.name.slice(3)]=s.id;\n     const T=async(chars,key,color)=>{const t=figma.createText();await t.setTextStyleIdAsync(TS[key]);t.characters=chars;t.fills=S(color);return t;};\n     const IF=h=>[{type:\"IMAGE\",imageHash:h,scaleMode:\"FIT\"}];\n     const GH=async id=>(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id)).fills[0].imageHash;\n     async function ic(id,color,size){const src=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);const i=src.createInstance();i.resize(size,size);const col=S(color);for(const n of i.findAll(x=>\"fills\"in x&&Array.isArray(x.fills)&&x.fills.length&&x.fills[0].type===\"SOLID\")){try{n.fills=col}catch(e){}}for(const n of i.findAll(x=>\"strokes\"in x&&Array.isArray(x.strokes)&&x.strokes.length&&x.strokes[0].type===\"SOLID\")){try{n.strokes=col}catch(e){}}return i;}\n     async function status(f,dark){const sb=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"49:130\")).createInstance();sb.fills=[];f.appendChild(sb);sb.x=0;sb.y=0;const col=dark?\"FFFFFF\":C.ink;for(const n of sb.findAll(n=>\"fills\"in n&&Array.isArray(n.fills)&&n.fills.length)){try{n.fills=S(col)}catch(e){}}return sb;}\n     async function hind(f,dark){const hi=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"49:141\")).createInstance();hi.fills=[];f.appendChild(hi);hi.x=0;hi.y=898;const bar=hi.findOne(n=>n.type===\"RECTANGLE\");if(bar)bar.fills=S(dark?\"FFFFFF\":C.ink);return hi;}\n     ```\n   - **Screen patterns used**: PriceBar 430×118 at y814, white, topLeft/topRightRadius 28, shadow y-6; contains Caption label + Price value + Button 1:473 instance at x206 y16 with findOne(TEXT).characters override, named \"OrderNowBtn\"/\"PrimaryBtn\". Product pages: HeaderBar instance at y44, glow ellipse 260 opacity 0.10 blur 90, product image clone 240 wide at x95 y~118, name Title/L at y400, rating row, desc Body mut 382 wide, Spicy chips, Portion stepper, PriceBar. Customize: exploded 1:244 clone 110×150, chips Hot selected, stepper count \"2\", toppings grid 4+3 (col*98, row*106, tile 88×96), sides row 5 (68+10.5 spacing, tile 68×96). Payment: summary card AL V (cardH 214), PayCredit/PayDebit instances at y434/522 with CardImg fill + Name/Number overrides, toggle row at y626. Overlay: clone of 2013:634 + Scrim rect (ink 0.55) + SuccessDialog 320 wide AL V (green circle 88 + check white 44, \"Success!\" Title/L, body, GoBackBtn). Chat: Messages wrap AL V gap 12 at (24,128), bubA/bubC instances with \"Text\" override (long texts HEIGHT+resize(238) — verify visually), customer bubbles layoutAlign=\"MAX\", timestamp Caption centered, InputBar with InputPill 322×56 + SendBtn.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **`set_layoutPositioning: Can only set layoutPositioning = ABSOLUTE if the parent node has layoutMode !== NONE`** (B2 attempt 1): badge frame's layoutPositioning was set before appendChild. Fixed by appending to the auto-layout component FIRST, then setting layoutPositioning=\"ABSOLUTE\".\n   - **`combineAsVariants: Grouped nodes must be in the same page as the parent`** (B2 attempt 2): components were created on figma.currentPage (\"00 · Start Here 设计任务\") not page 2003:2. Fixed by adding `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(P)` at the start of the call. (Established that ALL node-creating calls need this.)\n   - **Profile InfoCard overflow (cardH 353, buttons ended at y1001 > 932)**: address ProfileField instance had its Value text clamped to 38 wide → wrapped to 162 tall. First fix attempt (instance layoutSizingHorizontal=\"FIXED\" + resize, then Value textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\" + resize(342,20)) FAILED — instance child text geometry overrides don't stick. Final fix: removed the address instance and inserted a manually built \"AddressRow\" frame (AL V gap 4: Caption label + Body value with HEIGHT resize(342) → 1 line 20h). Card now 211 tall; Settings label y529, buttons y719, logout ends 859 < 898 ✓.\n   - **`set_reactions` schema validation error** (prototype call): reaction objects rejected. Error details: trigger \"AFTER_DELAY\" invalid → must be \"AFTER_TIMEOUT\" with `delay` property (not `timeout`); trigger enum lists ON_CLICK/ON_HOVER/ON_PRESS/ON_DRAG/ON_MEDIA_END (also MOUSE_*, ON_KEY_DOWN, ON_MEDIA_HIT); action `{type:\"NODE\",destinationId,navigation:\"NAVIGATE\"}` has an accepting branch BUT `transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\",duration:0.3}` fails — DISSOLVE not supported by this schema; valid transitions are MOVE_IN/MOVE_OUT/PUSH/SLIDE_IN/SLIDE_OUT with direction+easing+matchLayers required, or transition can be omitted/null. ON_TAP trigger is untested (error was raised on the first AFTER_DELAY splash link). The call rolled back atomically — NO prototype links exist yet.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - All 11 screens + full component library + design system built successfully in workspace page 2003:2.\n   - Solved page-targeting bug (setCurrentPageAsync), atomic rollback discovery (saves cleanup work), instance text override limitation (manual row rebuild), auto-layout badge positioning order.\n   - Profile overflow root-caused via probing (instance child 88w/180h) and fixed permanently.\n   - Remaining: prototype links (schema now understood), screenshot verification of all 11 screens, visual fixes, final answer.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Original request (from prior session, Chinese): “请在以下Figma文件中完成完整设计： Figma 文件：https://www.figma.com/design/HLFV6DkE9fZgeCIwE7fLvf/ 请先阅读「00·Start Here」中的设计任务，参考「01· Foundations」中的视觉规范，复用「02·Components」中的组件，使用「04·Media」中的素材，最终将完整设计交付至「03·Workspace」。\"\n   - Benchmark instructions (same turn): assigned file must be used exclusively; whoami must confirm fulinbo@tetras.ai; read 00·Start Here; follow 01·Foundations; reuse 02·Components and 04·Media; preserve all reference pages and their existing nodes; create complete design inside 03 · Workspace (create if missing; new frames/components/prototype connections allowed even if empty); starter read-only instructions apply to reference pages, not workspace; keep unrelated content intact; do not replace reference pages, create a different file, or switch accounts/teams; workflow whoami→get_metadata→read-only use_figma→use_figma build→get_screenshot verify; use valid Plugin API, load fonts before text; build in manageable sections; add prototype interactions after screens exist; inspect screenshots of all required screens, fix and re-check; finish with assigned file URL, 03·Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations; unattended session — resolve routine choices via brief, report actual limitations if blocked; prefix every tool call with \"Reasoning summary:\"; final response format \"Reasoning summary: ...\" then \"Final answer:\".\n   - (This session contained no new user messages — only the continuation instruction and tool results.)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Re-run prototype links with CORRECTED reaction schema:\n     - Splash 2011:147 → 2011:165 via `{trigger:{type:\"AFTER_TIMEOUT\",delay:2000},action:{type:\"NODE\",destinationId:\"2011:165\",navigation:\"NAVIGATE\"}}`\n     - ON_TAP links (try `{type:\"ON_TAP\"}` first; if rejected use `{type:\"ON_CLICK\"}`): card 2011:211→2012:313; 2011:232→2012:379; 2011:253→2012:445; 2011:274→2012:511; tabProfile I2011:295;2010:107→2014:693; tabSupport I2011:295;2010:120→2015:743; product backs (HeaderBar instance children[0] in 2012:313/379/445/511)→2011:165; 03 OrderNowBtn→2013:493; 07 back→2012:313; 07 PrimaryBtn 2013:630→2013:634; 08 back→2013:493; 08 PrimaryBtn 2013:709→2014:644; 09 GoBackBtn 2014:691→2011:165; 10 back I2014:705;2010:75→2011:165; 11 chat back (HeaderBar children[0])→2011:165. Do NOT add transition (or use a MOVE_* variant only if needed). Favourites tab and central Add get NO links (entry only). Order Now on 04–06 gets NO link.\n   - get_screenshot verification of ALL 11 screens (maxDimension ~1024–1400); check: Home greeting/chips fit (chipEnd 382 exact), chat bubble text sizing (msgsH 502 — long bubbles used the unreliable HEIGHT+resize on instance text; may need manual fix like Profile), product page layouts, customize tight spacing, overlay dialog centering, image fills correct.\n   - Fix any visual problems found; re-screenshot.\n   - Final answer with: file URL https://www.figma.com/design/HLFV6DkE9fZgeCIwE7fLvf/, page ID 2003:2, all 11 screen IDs, prototype summary, limitations (e.g., Favourites/Add entry-only, scrollable frames represented statically).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary, I ran the prototype-links use_figma call which FAILED on the first reaction assignment (`set_reactions` validation error). The intended link map was fully coded (16 links + splash auto-advance). The error revealed the correct schema: `AFTER_TIMEOUT` with `delay` (not AFTER_DELAY/timeout), and NODE actions cannot use DISSOLVE transitions in this MCP schema (transition must be omitted or MOVE_IN/MOVE_OUT/PUSH/SLIDE_IN/SLIDE_OUT with direction+easing+matchLayers). The failed call rolled back atomically, so no links were created. All 11 screens exist and are complete except for prototype wiring and visual verification.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Re-run the prototype links call with the corrected schema — per my last message: \"所有 11 个屏幕已建完，现在添加原型连接” (all 11 screens built, now adding prototype connections). Use:\n   ```js\n   const nav=(dest)=>[{trigger:{type:\"ON_TAP\"},action:{type:\"NODE\",destinationId:dest,navigation:\"NAVIGATE\"}}];\n   const delay=(dest,ms)=>[{trigger:{type:\"AFTER_TIMEOUT\",delay:ms},action:{type:\"NODE\",destinationId:dest,navigation:\"NAVIGATE\"}}];\n   ```\n   (no transition objects; fall back to `ON_CLICK` if `ON_TAP` is rejected, testing one node first). Then proceed to get_screenshot verification of all 11 screens and fix visual issues before the final answer.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /mnt/afs/gaoyongyong/code/rate_website_figma-sft-cc-tap-benchmark-design/storage/benchmarks/3case-7models-v4-20261028/r